   "summary": "The personal information of some 39,000 customers and employees has been leaked from Mirae Asset Securities Co., the securities firm said Saturday. Mirae Asset Securities, the country's leading brokerage house, said the account numbers of some 3,800 customers and the personal information of over 35,000 current and former employees, as well as contractors, were leaked. The data breach at Mirae Asset Securities is the latest in a series of data leaks in the financial sector.",
   "summary_zh": "证券经纪商Mirae Asset Securities周六表示，约39,000名客户和员工的个人信息遭泄露。Mirae Asset Securities是该国最大的证券经纪商，公司称，约3,800名客户的账户号码，以及超过35,000名现任和前任员工及承包商的个人信息遭到泄露。此次数据泄露是金融领域一系列数据泄露事件中的最新一起。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The personal information of some 39,000 customers and employees has been leaked from Mirae Asset Securities Co., the securities firm said Saturday. Mirae Asset Securities, the country's leading brokerage house, said the account numbers of some 3,800 customers and the personal information of over 35,000 current and former employees, as well as contractors, were leaked. The Korean brokerage said unauthorized external access occurred Wednesday and Thursday, targeting its mobile web phone authentication login service and internal system, respectively. The leaked non-customer, corporate data included names, employee ID numbers, email addresses, mobile phone numbers and passwords. Mirae Asset said it immediately blocked the affected access routes after detecting suspicious activity from external IP addresses and activated its emergency response system. The company also said it reported the incident to the Financial Services Commission, the Financial Supervisory Service and the Personal Information Protection Commission. The data breach came days after its sister companies, including Mirae Asset Life Insurance, suffered similar data leaks. The data breach at Mirae Asset Securities is the latest in a series of data leaks in the financial sector. According to the Financial Services Commission, more than 470,000 personal data records have been leaked from 37 companies across the financial sector over the past month, with the amount of funds stolen estimated at 1 billion won (US$745,000). Since Sept. 30, when the first data leak was detected, a total of 40 data leak incidents have been reported at 37 companies, including four commercial banks, five financial investment firms, three insurance firms and five savings banks, according to the regulator",
