   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription Congress Parliamentary Party (CPP) chairperson Sonia Gandhi’s promised memoir, Belonging: A Journey of Love, is among the most anticipated books in India this year — not only for its political content but also for the glimpse it offers into the private life of one of the country’s most ‘private’ public figures. But almost two decades before the memoir, Ms. Gandhi offered a rare account of her private world in a speech at the Netherlands-based Nexus Institute.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅即可解锁。国会人民党（CPP）主席索尼娅·甘地承诺推出的回忆录《归属：爱之旅》位居印度今年最受期待图书之列，不仅因为其政治内容，也因为它让人们得以窥见这位该国最注重“隐私”的公众人物之一的私人生活。然而，在这部回忆录问世近20年前，甘地女士曾在总部位于荷兰的Nexus Institute发表演讲，罕见地讲述了她的私人世界。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Congress Parliamentary Party (CPP) chairperson Sonia Gandhi’s promised memoir, Belonging: A Journey of Love, is among the most anticipated books in India this year — not only for its political content but also for the glimpse it offers into the private life of one of the country’s most ‘private’ public figures. She has promised that the book is bound to create a ‘tamasha’ as she tells her story in her own words. But almost two decades before the memoir, Ms. Gandhi offered a rare account of her private world in a speech at the Netherlands-based Nexus Institute. India / politics / Indian National Congress / books and literature Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
