   "ageDays": 0.04,
   "summary": "MANILA, Philippines – A United States envoy dismissed reports on Saturday, November 7, that a framework agreement for the US-backed Pax Silica Economic Security Zone would be signed during the 49th Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) Summit in Manila this month. “No such announcement on the Pax Silica Economic Security Zone was ever planned.",
   "summary_zh": "菲律宾马尼拉——美国特使周六驳斥了有关美国支持的“硅砂经济安全区”框架协议将于本月在马尼拉举行的第49届东盟峰会期间签署的报道。他表示：“从未计划就‘硅砂经济安全区’作出此类宣布。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Already have Rappler+? Sign in to listen to groundbreaking journalism. HOST. The welcome sign at the entrance of the Philippine International Convention Center complex and World Trade Center in Pasay City, on November 4, 2026. MANILA, Philippines – A United States envoy dismissed reports on Saturday, November 7, that a framework agreement for the US-backed Pax Silica Economic Security Zone would be signed during the 49th Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) Summit in Manila this month. “No such announcement on the Pax Silica Economic Security Zone was ever planned. Decisions will be made in full consultation with the government of the Philippines at the appropriate time,” US Ambassador to the Philippines Lee Lipton said in a statement. US President Donald Trump will be among the global leaders expected to attend the regional event. Envisioned as a massive 1,620-hectare industrial hub in New Clark City, Capas, Tarlac, the Pax Silica development is estimated by the BCDA to attract up to US$70 billion in investments and create as many as 190,000 direct jobs. The project, however, faces mounting criticisms in the Philippines, with many noting that the hub could harm the country’s environment, displace indigenous communities, and strain the Luzon energy grid because of its massive power and water needs, among others. “We look forward to working alongside the government of the Philippines about this exciting initiative to secure supply chains and attract quality investment in support of economic growth and jobs at home for the people,” Lipton said. – Rappler.com Upgrade to Rappler+ for exclusive content and unlimited access",
