   "_dt": 1794046789.0,
   "ageDays": 0.06,
   "summary": "Russia n forces hammered energy infrastructure around Ukraine's capital with missiles and drones overnight, straining Kyiv's power supply and heating systems as temperatures headed towards zero , officials said on Saturday. Explosions rocked the city as Russia fired multiple waves of ballistic missiles, several of which hit and damaged the Northern Bridge across the Dnipro River , according to Mayor Vitali Klitschko.",
   "summary_zh": "官员周六表示，俄罗斯夜间以导弹和无人机猛烈打击乌克兰首都周边的能源基础设施，导致基辅的供电和供暖系统承压，而气温正降至零度左右。据市长维塔利·克利奇科介绍，俄罗斯向这座城市发射了多轮弹道导弹，引发多次爆炸，其中数枚击中了第聂伯河上的北桥并造成损坏。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Russia n forces hammered energy infrastructure around Ukraine's capital with missiles and drones overnight, straining Kyiv's power supply and heating systems as temperatures headed towards zero , officials said on Saturday. Explosions rocked the city as Russia fired multiple waves of ballistic missiles, several of which hit and damaged the Northern Bridge across the Dnipro River , according to Mayor Vitali Klitschko. Strikes on energy facilities outside Kyiv — including systems sending power from two nuclear plants to the city and Ukraine's central regions — caused serious damage, the energy ministry said. \"The capital is facing serious difficulties with its electricity, water, and heat supplies,\" President Volodymyr Zelensky said on X, adding that substations in five other regions were also hit. He said Russia had launched 36 ballistic missiles, only four of which were intercepted, according to Ukraine's air force. It added that air defences had downed 149 out of 172 drones. At least two people were killed and around a dozen others wounded across Ukraine in the overnight attacks, which also damaged homes, businesses and non-residential buildings, authorities said. Moscow's defense ministry said it carried out a massive strike on what it described as targets in Ukraine's military-industrial sector, as well as energy and transport infrastructure in and around Kyiv. Russia has stepped up air attacks on Ukraine as its ground offensive has largely stalled, pounding energy infrastructure in major cities with difficult-to-intercept missiles and drones more than four-and-a-half years into its full-scale invasion. It has expanded its campaign in recent weeks to target Kyiv's bridges, snarling traffic in the city of more than 3 million people. \" Russia is preparing for trilateral talks by launching ballistic missiles at Ukraine's critical infrastructure,\" Zelensky said on X. The attacks also follow recent U.S. midterm elections that have raised hopes in Ukraine for stronger support against Russia 's war from a Democratic-controlled Congress. \"We are counting on the U.S. Congress to give more attention to Ukraine, because Russia keeps increasing the number of its attacks,\" Zelensky added. We are facing unprecedented challenges. Russia's Prosecutor General's Office has designated The Moscow Times as an \"undesirable\" organization, criminalizing our work and putting our staff at risk of prosecution. This follows our earlier unjust labeling as a \"foreign agent.\" These actions are direct attempts to silence independent journalism in Russia. The authorities claim our work \"discredits the decisions of the Russian leadership.\" We see things differently: we strive to provide accurate, unbiased reporting on Russia. We, the journalists of The Moscow Times, refuse to be silenced. But to continue our work, we need your help . Your support, no matter how small, makes a world of difference. If you can, please support us monthly starting from just $ 2. It's quick to set up, and every contribution makes a significant impact. By supporting The Moscow Times, you're defending open, independent journalism in the face of repression. Thank you for standing with us",
