   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription CPI(M) Tripura State Secretary Jitendra Chaudhury on Saturday (November 7, 2026) said the party was keen to forge an electoral understanding with democratic and secular parties to prevent a split in anti-BJP votes in the civic elections. His statement came a day after the deadline for filing nominations for elections to 21 civic bodies, including the Agartala Municipal Corporation (AMC), ended.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅即可解锁这些内容。印度人民党特里普拉邦负责人吉特伦德拉·乔杜里于2026年11月7日（星期六）表示，该党热衷于与民主派和世俗派政党达成选举协议，以避免在市政选举中出现反印度人民党选票分裂的情况。他发表这番言论的前一天，恰是包括阿加尔塔拉市政委员会（AMC）在内的21个市政机构选举候选人提名截止期限。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription CPI(M) Tripura State Secretary Jitendra Chaudhury on Saturday (November 7, 2026) said the party was keen to forge an electoral understanding with democratic and secular parties to prevent a split in anti-BJP votes in the civic elections. His statement came a day after the deadline for filing nominations for elections to 21 civic bodies, including the Agartala Municipal Corporation (AMC), ended. The CPI(M) has fielded 263 candidates across 345 wards, while the Congress has nominated candidates in 221 wards after seat-sharing talks between the two INDIA bloc partners failed. \"The date for filing nominations for the civic elections ended yesterday, and scrutiny has begun. We are still hopeful of a seat adjustment with anti-BJP parties, as defeating the saffron party is our main political objective,\" Mr. Chaudhury told reporters. Accusing the BJP of weakening democratic values in Tripura over the past nine years, the Leader of Opposition in the State Assembly said he had held discussions with the leadership of a major anti-BJP party on an electoral understanding. \"We emphasised seat adjustment with anti-BJP parties to avoid a split in the anti-BJP vote bank in the civic elections. A decision may be taken in the next two days, as the last date for withdrawal of nominations is November 10. The party is fully committed to preventing a split in anti-BJP votes in the State,\" he said. Meanwhile, Left Front convener Manik Dey on Friday (November 6, 2026) alleged that party candidates were unable to file nominations in five civic bodies, Santirbazar, Ranirbazar, Jirania, Mohanpur and Kamalpur, due to alleged obstruction by ruling party leaders and supporters. He also alleged that the police and the State Election Commission had failed to ensure security for Left Front candidates despite a Tripura High Court order. Mr. Dey further claimed that five party supporters were injured in an attack by BJP supporters at Dukli in West Tripura district while campaigning for CPI(M) candidate Swapna Nath, who is contesting from AMC Ward 44. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
