   "title": "Nigerian wins US fellowship",
   "url": "https://punchng.com/nigerian-wins-us-fellowship/",
   "domain": "punchng.com",
   "source": "Punch（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Sat, 07 Nov 2026 01:43:53 +0000",
   "_dt": 1794015833.0,
   "ageDays": 0.42,
   "summary": "An Interdisciplinary Humanities doctoral candidate at the University of California, Omowumi Omole, has been awarded the 2026 Dean’s Dissertation Fellowship from the School of Social Sciences, Humanities and Arts. The fellowship, valued at $27,000, will support her dissertation fieldwork and data collection in Lagos, Nigeria. In a statement made available to Diaspora Tales, the fellowship is designed to help doctoral candidates make steady progress on their dissertations.",
   "summary_zh": "加利福尼亚大学跨学科人文学科博士候选人奥莫武米·奥莫莱获颁社会科学、人文学科与艺术学院2026年院长论文奖学金。这项价值27,000美元的奖学金将支持她在尼日利亚拉各斯开展论文田野调查和数据收集。Diaspora Tales获得的声明称，该奖学金旨在帮助博士候选人稳步推进论文研究。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "An Interdisciplinary Humanities doctoral candidate at the University of California, Omowumi Omole, has been awarded the 2026 Dean’s Dissertation Fellowship from the School of Social Sciences, Humanities and Arts. The fellowship, valued at $27,000, will support her dissertation fieldwork and data collection in Lagos, Nigeria. In a statement made available to Diaspora Tales, the fellowship is designed to help doctoral candidates make steady progress on their dissertations. “It releases Omole from her teaching responsibilities for the Fall 2026 semester so that she can devote her full attention to research,” it stated. “Omole’s dissertation examines how Pentecostal marriage teachings shape women’s political subjectivity, particularly their views on laws meant to protect them from violence. “Her work looks closely at the debate over the non-criminalisation of marital rape in Nigeria, a debate that gained fresh attention after the widely publicised death of gospel singer Osinachi Nwachukwu.” Her ethnographic study follows women through marriage classes at two Lagos churches and examines churchgoers’ attitudes towards issues such as bodily autonomy and reproductive rights. Omole has also conducted research among Nigerian diaspora congregations in Dallas, Texas, and plans to continue the study at a church in Houston, to see how the same teachings are embodied abroad. Biodun Busari Biodun Busari is a journalist at Punch Newspapers with five years of experience reporting on human interest, crime, diaspora issues, and feature storytelling. He focuses on producing engaging, informative stories that enlighten the public and provide context on complex topics. Biodun’s work demonstrates hands-on newsroom experience and a strong commitment to accurate, purpose-driven journalism",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "ng"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "sec",
    "pol"
   ],
   "tier": 2,
   "actor": "美国",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "cnHit": false,
   "usHit": true,
   "terrHit": false,
   "riskHit": false,
   "riskKind": "",
   "score": 0.6,
   "tag": "rss_punchng",
   "title_zh": "尼日利亚人获得美国研究员奖学金",
   "body_zh": "加州大学跨学科人文学科博士生奥莫武米·奥莫勒获社会科学、人文与艺术学院授予的2026年院长论文研究奖学金。这项价值$27,000的奖学金将支持她在尼日利亚（国家，首都阿布贾）拉各斯开展论文实地调查和数据收集。Diaspora Tales获得的一份声明称，该奖学金旨在帮助博士生稳步推进论文写作。声明说：“这使奥莫勒在2026年秋季学期无需承担教学任务，从而能够全身心投入研究。奥莫勒的论文探讨五旬节婚姻教义如何塑造女性的政治主体性，尤其是她们对旨在保护其免遭暴力的法律的认识。她的研究 closely 关注尼日利亚（国家，首都阿布贾）关于婚内强奸非刑事化的辩论；在福音歌手奥西纳奇·纳丘库广受关注的死亡事件后，这场辩论再次受到关注。”她的民族志研究跟踪女性参加拉各斯两所教堂的婚姻课程，并考察信众对身体自主权和生育权利等问题的态度。奥莫勒还曾在得克萨斯州达拉斯的尼日利亚侨民教会中开展研究，并计划继续在休斯敦的一所教堂开展调查，以观察同样的教义在海外如何得到践行。比奥敦·布萨里是Punch Newspapers记者，拥有5年报道民生、犯罪、侨民议题和特稿故事的经验。他专注于创作生动 informative、启迪公众并为复杂议题提供背景的故事。比奥敦的工作展现了扎实的新闻编辑室经验，以及对准确、以目的为导向的新闻业的坚定承诺。",
   "snippet_zh": ""
