   "title": "ADC Ruling: AA Presidential Candidate Warns Of Threat To Nigeria’s Democracy",
   "url": "https://leadership.ng/adc-ruling-aa-presidential-candidate-warns-of-threat-to-nigerias-democracy/",
   "domain": "leadership.ng",
   "source": "Leadership（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Fri, 06 Nov 2026 11:38:23 +0000",
   "_dt": 1793965103.0,
   "ageDays": 1.01,
   "summary": "The AA presidential candidate, in a statement on Friday, November 6, 2026, described the Federal High Court judgment nullifying the leadership of the African Democratic Congress (ADC) under former Senate President David Mark and invalidating the presidential nomination of former Vice President Atiku Abubakar as troubling.",
   "summary_zh": "该党总统候选人在2026年11月6日星期五发表的声明中称，联邦高等法院裁定非洲民主大会（ADC）由前参议院议长戴维·马克领导的领导层无效，并使前副总统阿提库·阿布巴卡尔的总统提名无效，此举令人不安。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "He cautioned that the development could set a dangerous precedent for opposition politics, insisting that every political party and candidate had a stake in protecting democratic participation and the people’s right to choose their leaders. The AA presidential candidate, in a statement on Friday, November 6, 2026, described the Federal High Court judgment nullifying the leadership of the African Democratic Congress (ADC) under former Senate President David Mark and invalidating the presidential nomination of former Vice President Atiku Abubakar as troubling. He said the timing of the judgment, barely two and a half months before the 2027 general elections, had raised serious questions about judicial independence, political competition and the future of Nigeria’s democracy. Fadojoe stressed that his reaction was not based on party affiliation, noting that he was not a member of the ADC but believed that an injustice against democratic participation in one party could threaten the rights of other opposition candidates. On the role of the judiciary, Fadojoe acknowledged the importance of the courts in upholding the Constitution and ensuring that political actors operate within the law. “Why has Nigeria become a country where political parties spend more time defending their existence in courtrooms than presenting solutions to the Nigerian people?” he queried. He also questioned why elections were increasingly becoming entangled in prolonged litigation, factional disputes and last-minute judicial pronouncements. The AA presidential candidate maintained that no political party or candidate should be above the law, but insisted that judicial decisions must take into account their broader implications for democratic participation. Fadojoe consequently called for urgent measures to restore public confidence in the independence, consistency and impartiality of the Nigerian judicial system. He urged President Tinubu and the APC to recognise that Nigerians were closely monitoring developments within the country’s political landscape. He maintained that the survival of Nigeria’s democracy depended on protecting political plurality, strengthening democratic institutions and ensuring that voters, rather than institutional controversies, ultimately determined the country’s political leadership. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates →",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "ng"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "pol"
   ],
   "tier": 3,
   "actor": "当事国政府",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "cnHit": false,
   "usHit": false,
   "terrHit": false,
   "riskHit": false,
   "riskKind": "",
   "score": 0.6,
   "tag": "rss_leadership",
   "title_zh": "ADC裁定：人民进步党总统候选人警告尼日利亚民主面临威胁",
   "body_zh": "他警告称，这一裁决可能为反对派政治树立危险先例，并坚持认为，每个政党和候选人都肩负着保护民主参与以及人民选择领导人的权利的责任。AA总统候选人在2026年11月6日星期五发表的声明中，将联邦高等法院撤销非洲民主大会（ADC）由前参议院议长David Mark领导的领导层，并使前副总统Atiku Abubakar的总统候选人资格无效的判决描述为令人不安。他说，在距离2027年大选仅两个半月之际作出这一判决，引发了人们对司法独立、政治竞争以及尼日利亚民主未来的严重质疑。Fadojoe强调，他的反应并非基于党派归属；他指出自己不是ADC成员，但认为，针对一个政党民主参与的不公可能威胁其他反对派候选人的权利。在谈到司法机构的作用时，Fadojoe承认法院在维护宪法、确保政治行为参与者在法律框架内活动方面的重要性。“为什么尼日利亚会变成这样一个国家：各政党花在法庭上捍卫自身存在的时间，反而多于向尼日利亚人民提出解决方案的时间？”他质问道。他还质疑，为什么选举日益与旷日持久的诉讼、派系争端以及司法机构在最后时刻作出的裁决交织在一起。AA总统候选人坚持认为，任何政党或候选人都不得凌驾于法律之上，但强调司法决定必须考虑其对民主参与的更广泛影响。因此，Fadojoe呼吁采取紧急措施，恢复公众对尼日利亚司法体系独立性、一致性和公正性的信心。他敦促Tinubu总统和APC正视尼日利亚人民正在密切关注国内政治局势的发展。他坚持认为，尼日利亚民主能否存续，取决于保护政治多元性、强化民主制度，并确保最终决定国家政治领导层的是选民，而非制度争议。我们掌握独家优势。获取实时报道、突发独家内幕和独家视角，直接推送到您的手机。不要满足于过时新闻。加入LEADERSHIP NEWS的WhatsApp，随时随地接收24/7最新消息→",
   "snippet_zh": ""
