   "title": "Amish Shah claims victory in Arizona, sixth Indian-American in U.S. House",
   "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/amish-shah-claims-victory-in-arizona-sixth-indian-american-in-us-house/article71668702.ece",
   "domain": "thehindu.com",
   "source": "thehindu.com",
   "published": "Thu, 05 Nov 2026 13:41:10 +0530",
   "_dt": 1793866270.0,
   "ageDays": 2.15,
   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription Indian-American physician Amish Shah has made history after becoming the first from the community to represent Arizona in Congress. Dr. Shah, 48, claimed victory in the election for the U.S. House of Representatives from Arizona's First Congressional District on Wednesday (Novembner 4, 2026). Dr. Shah became the sixth Indian American to be elected to the U.S. House of Representatives.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅即可解锁 印度裔美国医生阿米什·沙阿创造历史，成为首位代表亚利桑那州进入国会的该社群人士。48岁的沙阿博士于2026年11月4日星期三在亚利桑那州第一国会选区的美国众议院选举中宣布获胜。沙阿博士成为第六位当选美国众议员的印度裔美国人。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Indian-American physician Amish Shah has made history after becoming the first from the community to represent Arizona in Congress. Dr. Shah, 48, claimed victory in the election for the U.S. House of Representatives from Arizona's First Congressional District on Wednesday (Novembner 4, 2026). \"Arizona, it's the honour of a lifetime to be your next congressman,\" Dr. Shah said in a post on X on Wednesday (November 4, 2-026). Dr. Shah became the sixth Indian American to be elected to the U.S. House of Representatives. Arizona, it's the honor of a lifetime to be your next congressman. https://t.co/RUzwWJWF2B Dr. Shah, a three-term member of the Arizona House of Representatives, defeated Republican Jay Feely, a former National Football League player, who was endorsed by President Donald Trump. Dr. Shah and Mr. Feely were locked in a close battle, with the Democrat bagging 52.49%of the vote against his rival’s 45.45%. Decision Desk HQ called the race at 8:39 p.m. EST on Wednesday (November 4, 2026). “It's not easy running for public office, and I commend Jay Feely on a hard-fought race,” Dr. Shah said. “To every voter in this district — I pledge to be a Representative for all of you, whether or not you voted for me,” he said. Dr. Shah made history as he became the first Indian-American to represent Arizona in Congress. By defeating Mr. Feely, Dr. Shah flipped a Republican-held seat. Dr. Shah “has been a champion for Arizonans since 2019 when he was first elected to the AZ House of Representatives. Now, he'll take the fight to Washington, DC to fight for working families,” the Indian American Impact said. Chintan Patel, Executive Director of Indian American Impact, said Dr. Shah earned this seat one conversation at a time. \"He knocked on more than 28,000 doors and talked with voters across this district about what they’re facing: health care they can’t afford and costs that keep climbing. As an emergency room doctor, he has seen firsthand what unaffordable care does to families, and he ran to lower those costs.\" Now on opposite sides of the political spectrum, Dr. Shah and Mr. Feely have a shared history. The Democratic candidate was the NFL physician providing emergency care to the New York Jets — the team for which Feely was the kicker. Born in Chicago to Gujarati parents who immigrated to the U.S. in the 1960s, Dr., Shah earned his undergraduate degree at Northwestern University and his medical degree at Northwestern University Medical School as part of the Honours Program in Medical Education. He received a full merit scholarship to obtain a Master’s in Public Health at the University of California, Berkeley, followed by residency training in Emergency Medicine at New York City's busiest Level-1 trauma centre. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "in"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "pol"
   ],
   "tier": 2,
   "actor": "美国",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "cnHit": false,
